## Reading the deck count

Mono-B and mono-R cards top the ranking because more of the 25 Mardu-wedge archetypes are mono- or include those colors. A B/R land slots into 9 of 25 archetypes, 3 Rakdos sub-archetypes plus 3 Mardu sub-archetypes plus 3 mono-B builds. A W/R land slots into only 6 because W/R has the fewest current Standard archetypes in the wedge.

The math says crafting mythics wins more decks per wildcard. Practically, mono-B Liliana and Bloodthirsty Conqueror sit inside the color-identity range of 18 archetypes, not that they are auto-played in all 18 builds. Each Mardu-wedge deck still wants fixing first, and your fixing is already 19 of the 22 W/B/R duals at 4-of. The shocks (Blood Crypt, Godless Shrine, Sacred Foundry) cover 9 + 8 + 6 = 23 archetype-slots in the W/B/R duals layer, where you currently have zero.

